# One maintainer, so this file is not about routing. It exists so that the
# files with a rule attached to them cannot be changed without the rule's
# author seeing it — the twins that drift, the lists that are contracts, and
# the things CI cannot check.

# Everything, by default.
*                           @bmachek

# CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md must stay identical from line 4 down, and
# `tools/check-docs.sh` is what says so. A change to the checker is a change to
# the only thing holding the twins together.
/CLAUDE.md                  @bmachek
/AGENTS.md                  @bmachek
/tools/check-docs.sh        @bmachek

# The two fetch scripts are twins as well: the material and sound lists are the
# contract and only the shell plumbing may differ between them.
/tools/fetch-materials.sh   @bmachek
/tools/fetch-materials.bat  @bmachek

# The one non-CC0 asset in the tree. ODbL, and CREDITS.md carries the
# attribution the licence requires.
/assets/cities/             @bmachek
/CREDITS.md                 @bmachek
/LICENSE                    @bmachek

# Determinism lives here: the RNG streams and the chunk index. A shared stream
# or a reused key silently reshuffles the whole city.
/src/core/rng.rs            @bmachek
/src/world/streaming.rs     @bmachek

# CI and release. A change here changes what "it passed" means.
/.github/                   @bmachek
